<title>BRAZIL: Sao Paulo April unemployment at 15.9 pct - Dieese.</title>
<headline>Sao Paulo April unemployment at 15.9 pct - Dieese.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The unemployment rate in Sao Paulo city was steady at 15.9 percent, the same rate as in April 1996, the Labor Union Statistics Institute (Dieese) reported.</p>
<p>The number of unemployed workers, however, rose to 1.359 million, up from 1.342 million in the same month last year, it said.</p>
<p>April figures also rose against March 1997, when the number of unemployed workers was 15.0 percent of the workforce, or 1.263 million workers, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 2485418))</p>
